From: ESP32-S31 Linux port
Subject: [PATCH] os: fix the arc4random_buf fallback so it builds on musl

Two bugs in the same seven lines, both reachable only when the C library has
getrandom() but not arc4random_buf() - which is exactly musl here:

  - the loop tests `pos < len`, and there is no `len`; the parameter is
    `nbytes`.  glibc builds never notice because they take the
    HAVE_ARC4RANDOM_BUF path and the fallback is not compiled.
  - getrandom() is called without including <sys/random.h>, so it is an
    implicit declaration, which -Werror=implicit turns into an error.

Signed-off-by: ESP32-S31 Linux port
---
--- a/os/osdep.h
+++ b/os/osdep.h
@@ -85,12 +85,16 @@
 
 /* for platforms lacking arc4random_buf() libc function */
 #ifndef HAVE_ARC4RANDOM_BUF
+#ifdef HAVE_GETRANDOM
+#include <sys/random.h>
+#endif
+
 static inline void arc4random_buf(void *buf, size_t nbytes)
 {
 #ifdef HAVE_GETRANDOM
     ssize_t pos = 0;
-    while (pos < len) {
-        ssize_t ret = getrandom(buf + pos, nbytes - pos, 0);
+    while (pos < (ssize_t) nbytes) {
+        ssize_t ret = getrandom((unsigned char *) buf + pos, nbytes - pos, 0);
         if (ret <= 0) {
             if (ret < 0 && errno == EINTR)
                 continue;
